---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/innerpage-common.astro";
const title =
	"Optimizely product recommendation redesign - Portfolio of Manaj Chakrobarti";
const bodyClass = "works";
import "../../styles/workspages.scss";
import Comparison from "../../layouts/components/comparison.astro";
---

<PageLayout title={title} bodyClass={bodyClass}>
	<main class="box workspage">
		<header class="inner section-header">
			<h1>
				Redesigning self-service widgets for product recommendations
			</h1>
			<article class="project-information">
				<div class="contributions">
					<h2>My Contributions</h2>
					<ul class="no-list">
						<li>UX/UI Design</li>
						<li>Design System</li>
						<li>Research & Testing</li>
						<li>Heuristic Evaluation</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<section class="details">
					<div class="challange">
						<h2>Challenge</h2>
						<p>
							Optimizely Recommendation was part of their
							personalization offering and was acquired from
							Peerius in 2016. The software had an outdated design
							and was primarily a managed solution. The goal was
							to improve its UX and usability to transition it
							into a self-service platform.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="team">
						<h2>Team</h2>
						<p>
							I worked as the lead product designer based in
							Dhaka, collaborating with our PM in the USA and the
							development team in Vietnam.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="discover">
						<h2>Approch</h2>
						<p>
							I started with a heuristic evaluation, then met with
							two product veterans to learn about the software,
							its terminology, functionality, and mapped existing
							user flows.
						</p>
						<p>
							Together with the PM, I defined the scope for
							redesigning widget management, a core part of the
							app that manages recommendation algorithms. We
							planned user validation and a prototype aligned with
							the Optimizely design system, which was new to me at
							the time.
						</p>
						<p>
							Then I collaborated with the research team to
							recruit participants and conducted unmoderated
							usability testing. I used the positive feedback and
							suggestions for improvement to inform the next
							iteration.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="solution">
						<h2>Solution</h2>
						<p>
							Refined the design based on previous testing and
							issues found during development. I also created a
							clickable prototype to guide implementation.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="outcome">
						<h2>Outcome</h2>
						<p>
							The redesigned widget management experience moved
							into development for the Alpha release. User testing
							provided positive feedback and identified
							opportunities for improvement. My iterative
							prototypes and detailed design specifications helped
							align the experience with user needs and support
							implementation by the development team.
						</p>

						<h2>Learning</h2>
						<p>
							I learned that users often prefer familiar, reliable
							software, while companies look for modern solutions.
							It also taught me to consider the entire system, not
							just individual parts.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>
			</article>
		</header>

		<section class="inner before-after">
			<h2>The Redesign</h2>
			<Comparison
				before="/images/works/opti-product-recommendation-suite/self-service-widget-before.png"
				after="/images/works/opti-product-recommendation-suite/self_service_widget.png"
				beforeAlt="Previous design of optimizely widgets page"
				afterAlt="Optimizely product recommendation redesign"
			/>
		</section>

		<section class="inner">
			<h2>The Experience in Action</h2>
			<article>
				<figure>
					<video controls width="250">
						<source
							src="/images/works/opti-product-recommendation-suite/self_service.webm"
							type="video/webm"
						/>Download the <a
							href="/images/works/opti-product-recommendation-suite/self-serving-widgets-final.mov"
							>Mov file</a
						>
					</video>
				</figure>
			</article>
		</section>
		<a href="/" id="back"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i></a>
	</main>
</PageLayout>
